ARTICLE = '<!doctype html><html lang="en-US"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Azure virtual server pricing: scoped compute and billing states | VPS Cost Lens</title><meta name="description" content="Azure VM compute prices fixed to East US, Standard_D2s_v5, Linux and purchase type, with 730-hour estimates, state billing checks and separate backup meters."><link rel="canonical" href="https://vpscostlens.com/pricing/azure-virtual-server/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="./page.css"></head><body><header><a href="/">VPS Cost Lens</a><span>Official-source price index</span></header><main><h1>azure virtual server pricing</h1><p><strong>There is no single whole-server price without a defined configuration.</strong> In <strong>eastus</strong>, <strong>Standard_D2s_v5</strong>, <strong>Linux base compute without a paid image licence</strong>, <strong>Consumption / pay-as-you-go</strong>, the compute rate is <strong>$0.096/hour</strong> [C.retailPrice]. At <strong>730 hours</strong> assumed usage, that is <strong>$70.08/month estimated compute cost</strong> [C.retailPrice × 730]. Disks, networking, backup and other chosen services require separate inputs; no whole-server total is quoted.</p><h2>Pay-as-you-go compute: fixed region, SKU, OS and purchase type</h2><p>USD retail meter, excluding Spot, Low Priority and Dev/Test records. O: the API has no operating-system field. We select the exact base product <code>Virtual Machines Dsv5 Series</code> and exact standard SKU, excluding the separate Windows product. Microsoft explains that this compute meter is the Linux meter; a Windows licence is separate [O, opening paragraphs of <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/prepay-reserved-vm-instances">Save costs with Azure Reserved VM Instances</a>]. The OS scope here is Linux with no paid image or software licence.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th scope="col">Region</th><th scope="col">VM SKU</th><th scope="col">OS scope</th><th scope="col">Purchase type</th><th scope="col">Official hourly rate</th><th scope="col">730-hour monthly estimate</th></tr><tr><td><code>eastus</code> [armRegionName]</td><td><code>Standard_D2s_v5</code> [armSkuName]</td><td>Linux base compute; no paid image licence [O]</td><td>Consumption / PAYG [C.type]</td><td>$0.096/hour [C.retailPrice; C.unitOfMeasure]</td><td>$0.096 × 730 assumed hours = <strong>$70.08, estimate</strong></td></tr></table></div><p class="source-note">Data source: official Microsoft Retail Prices API · 2026-11-12 14:25 UTC · <a href="https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?%24filter=serviceName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines%27+and+armRegionName+eq+%27eastus%27+and+armSkuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+productName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines+Dsv5+Series%27+and+skuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+priceType+eq+%27Consumption%27&amp;currencyCode=USD">Exact API query</a>. C selects the sole returned Items record. The monthly amount is calculated, not an official monthly tariff.</p><h2>Reservation records, kept separate from pay-as-you-go</h2><p>These are API-listed reservation amounts paired with their returned terms, not hourly quotes or whole-server totals. The response reports <code>unitOfMeasure = 1 Hour</code> even on these reservation records. We preserve that metadata and show <code>retailPrice</code> with <code>reservationTerm</code>; we do not derive a reservation hourly or monthly price from that label. Payment timing and a personalized purchase quote are not established by this response. Microsoft describes reservation payment options and compute-only coverage in [R, opening paragraphs and Buy a Reserved VM Instance, first paragraph].</p><h3>Reservation — 1 Year</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th scope="col">Region</th><th scope="col">VM SKU</th><th scope="col">OS scope</th><th scope="col">Purchase type and term</th><th scope="col">Returned retail amount</th><th scope="col">Returned unit metadata</th></tr><tr><td><code>eastus</code> [armRegionName]</td><td><code>Standard_D2s_v5</code> [armSkuName]</td><td>Linux base compute; no paid image licence [O]</td><td>Reservation; 1 Year [R1.type; R1.reservationTerm]</td><td>USD 519.00 [R1.retailPrice]</td><td><code>1 Hour</code> [unitOfMeasure]; not used as an hourly quote</td></tr></table></div><p class="source-note">Data source: official Microsoft Retail Prices API · 2026-11-12 14:25 UTC · <a href="https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?%24filter=serviceName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines%27+and+armRegionName+eq+%27eastus%27+and+armSkuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+productName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines+Dsv5+Series%27+and+skuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+priceType+eq+%27Reservation%27&amp;currencyCode=USD">Exact API query</a>. This table contains only this reservation term; no Consumption, Spot or Dev/Test prices are mixed into it.</p><h3>Reservation — 3 Years</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th scope="col">Region</th><th scope="col">VM SKU</th><th scope="col">OS scope</th><th scope="col">Purchase type and term</th><th scope="col">Returned retail amount</th><th scope="col">Returned unit metadata</th></tr><tr><td><code>eastus</code> [armRegionName]</td><td><code>Standard_D2s_v5</code> [armSkuName]</td><td>Linux base compute; no paid image licence [O]</td><td>Reservation; 3 Years [R2.type; R2.reservationTerm]</td><td>USD 997.00 [R2.retailPrice]</td><td><code>1 Hour</code> [unitOfMeasure]; not used as an hourly quote</td></tr></table></div><p class="source-note">Data source: official Microsoft Retail Prices API · 2026-11-12 14:25 UTC · <a href="https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?%24filter=serviceName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines%27+and+armRegionName+eq+%27eastus%27+and+armSkuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+productName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines+Dsv5+Series%27+and+skuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+priceType+eq+%27Reservation%27&amp;currencyCode=USD">Exact API query</a>. This table contains only this reservation term; no Consumption, Spot or Dev/Test prices are mixed into it.</p><h2>Same VM, different power state: the bill does not stop everywhere</h2><p>This checklist applies to the <strong>eastus / Standard_D2s_v5 / Linux base compute / PAYG</strong> scope above. The scenario keeps the VM in the named state for 730 assumed hours. Calculations cover only VM instance usage, not the entire bill.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th scope="col">Power state</th><th scope="col">Instance-usage billing</th><th scope="col">730-hour state scenario: compute only</th><th scope="col">Other bill checks</th></tr><tr><td>Running</td><td>Billed [S, Running row]</td><td>$0.096 × 730 = <strong>$70.08, estimate</strong></td><td>Disks and networking are separate; retained backup data remains billable [S footnote; B, Backup costs].</td></tr><tr><td>Stopped, still allocated</td><td>Billed [S, Stopped row]</td><td>$0.096 × 730 = <strong>$70.08, estimate</strong></td><td>A guest-OS shutdown can leave the allocation billed; disks/networking and retained backups are still separate [S, Stopped row and footnote; B].</td></tr><tr><td>Stopped and deallocated</td><td>Instance usage not billed [S, Deallocated row]</td><td>$0.096 × 0 billable instance hours = <strong>$0.00, estimate</strong></td><td>Disks/networking can continue; retaining vault backup data continues backup billing [S footnote; B]. This is not a zero-total bill.</td></tr></table></div><p class="source-note">Data source: official Microsoft Retail Prices API · 2026-11-12 14:25 UTC · <a href="https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?%24filter=serviceName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines%27+and+armRegionName+eq+%27eastus%27+and+armSkuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+productName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines+Dsv5+Series%27+and+skuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+priceType+eq+%27Consumption%27&amp;currencyCode=USD">Exact API query</a>. The API supplies only the reference compute rate. State rules come from <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/states-billing">S: Microsoft Learn, Power states and billing</a>, named rows and the footnote immediately below the table; backup persistence comes from B.</p><p>S describes the Stopped state as <q>The virtual machine is allocated on a host but not running.</q> Its footnote states <q>Some Azure resources, such as Disks and Networking continue to incur charges.</q></p><p>A reservation is a separate billing commitment: deallocation can leave unused reservation hours, or the benefit can move to another matching resource. Do not apply the PAYG zero-instance-usage result as a cancellation of a reservation purchase [U, How reservation discount is applied, opening paragraphs].</p><h2>Backup: protected-instance units and stored GB are separate</h2><p>Backup scenario: protect the same Linux VM workload in eastus using the consumption-priced Azure VM backup meter and Standard LRS vault storage. <strong>Analyst assumptions:</strong> one billable protected-instance meter unit for a month and 100 GB-month of stored backup data. A billable meter unit is not automatically a physical VM of any size: this example does not assert a protected-data size band or size a policy. Actual protected-instance units must be established from the workload and policy. The stored amount is retained recovery-point data, not the VM RAM, provisioned disk capacity or protected-data size [B, Backup costs].</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th scope="col">Region / purchase type</th><th scope="col">Backup SKU and meter</th><th scope="col">Protected workload OS</th><th scope="col">Official unit rate</th><th scope="col">Separate scenario calculation</th></tr><tr><td>eastus / Consumption [B1.armRegionName; B1.type]</td><td>Azure VM / Azure VM Protected Instance [B1.skuName; B1.meterName]</td><td>Linux Standard_D2s_v5; analyst workload scope</td><td>$10.00 per billable unit/month [B1.retailPrice; B1.unitOfMeasure]</td><td>1 assumed unit × $10.00 = <strong>$10.00/month, estimate</strong></td></tr><tr><td>eastus / Consumption [B2.armRegionName; B2.type]</td><td>Standard / Standard LRS Data Stored [B2.skuName; B2.meterName]</td><td>Same Linux workload; backup storage meter is OS-neutral</td><td>$0.0224 per GB-month [B2.retailPrice; B2.unitOfMeasure]</td><td>100 assumed GB-month × $0.0224 = <strong>$2.24/month, estimate</strong></td></tr></table></div><p class="source-note">Data source: official Microsoft Retail Prices API · 2026-11-12 14:22 UTC · <a href="https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?%24filter=serviceName+eq+%27Backup%27+and+armRegionName+eq+%27eastus%27+and+priceType+eq+%27Consumption%27&amp;currencyCode=USD">Exact API query</a>. B1 and B2 identify exact meterId records in the downloadable evidence. These are independent components, not a percentage surcharge or a whole-server total.</p><p>B, Backup costs, paragraph beginning Billing does not start: <q>Billing continues as long as any backup data for the VM is stored in a vault.</q> The following paragraph explains when stopping protection and deleting backup data stop billing. Stopping compute alone does not meet that condition.</p><h2>Official sources, record selectors and freshness</h2><ul><li><a href="https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices?%24filter=serviceName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines%27+and+armRegionName+eq+%27eastus%27+and+armSkuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+productName+eq+%27Virtual+Machines+Dsv5+Series%27+and+skuName+eq+%27Standard_D2s_v5%27+and+priceType+eq+%27Consumption%27&amp;currencyCode=USD">C</a>: sole Items record; all displayed C values are retailPrice, currencyCode, unitOfMeasure, armRegionName, armSkuName, productName, skuName and type.</li><li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/prepay-reserved-vm-instances">R</a>: opening paragraphs identify Linux/base compute and excluded Windows software; Buy a Reserved VM Instance, opening paragraph describes payment options.</li><li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/states-billing">S</a>: Power states and billing: Running, Stopped and Deallocated rows, plus the footnote directly below.</li><li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/backup-azure-vms-introduction">B</a>: Backup costs: paragraph beginning Billing does not start; next paragraph; protected-instance calculation paragraph; final paragraph on storage across recovery points.</li><li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/understand-vm-reservation-charges">U</a>: How reservation discount is applied, opening paragraphs: unused hours and deallocation.</li><li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/cost-management/retail-prices/azure-retail-prices">API documentation</a>: API response examples with reservation prices; API property details; API filters.</li></ul><p>R1 and R2 select the reservation Items records by <code>reservationTerm</code> and <code>meterId</code>, with the exact region, base product, standard SKU and type filters shown in each query. B1 selects <code>Azure VM Protected Instance</code>; B2 selects <code>Standard LRS Data Stored</code>. Their full meter IDs, source fields and retrieval times are in <a href="./sources.json">the timestamped evidence</a>.</p><p>730 hours, the state-duration examples, one backup billing unit and 100 GB-month are labelled scenario inputs. No actual calendar-month length or full invoice is inferred. Unverified disk/IP/network rates, paid-image licences, protected-size-band mapping, private discounts and account-specific taxes are omitted. No unknown field is labelled N/A.</p></main><footer>VPS Cost Lens · Independent price research</footer></body></html>'
